{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Before you came and I blessed him — indeed, he shall remain blessed</b>: It is not the way of one trembling with a very great trembling and crying out, \"Who is he that deceived me in order to bless him?\" that he should immediately conclude his outcry by saying \"indeed, he shall remain blessed\" — rather, it would have been fitting for him to curse him. Moreover, Esau was crying out to him, saying, \"Why then do you bless him now, my father?\" — so how could Esao believe that it had been by deception at the outset, when he sees that now he blesses him willingly? Now the correct interpretation in my eyes is that it is in the present tense: he says, Who then is the one who hunted game, who was able to deceive me into blessing him, and who will further be blessed in any event, for I know that he is blessed? Or the meaning of \"indeed, he shall remain blessed\" is: against my will — it is impossible for me to transfer the blessing from him, for from the moment I blessed him I knew through the holy spirit that his blessing had taken effect upon him. And this is the reason for the great trembling with which he trembled: for he knew that he had caused his beloved son to lose his blessing forever. And this is the meaning of \"Your brother came with deception\" — for after he said \"Who then?\", he set his mind that the one who had come to him was Jacob, for it is impossible that the blessing could rest except upon his seed:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:58.167151731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}